							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">I highly doubt eq has anywhere near 450 k +/- subscribers. We all have played eq in its hey day and sony is claiming they had 550,000 subscribers. Now everyone knows who has played the game when the servers were crowded that you could log in the middle of the day and see most every zone slam full of players, and during the peek times raid zones, grind zones, bazaar or selling area ( east commons) were jam packed with peeps. When I left, about 6 months ago, you were lucky to see over 20 people in one of the latest farm zones grinding. Game play was so off they had to merge servers and from what I had read some of those servers lacked alot more people than Rodcet. If I had to bet on the number of subcribers I would think the 450,000 subs were accounts still in thier data base, and paying subcribers would be more like 200,000 if that.I am sure there will be a core base of players for a long time to come but I personally think that games that take HUGE amounts of time are going to be on the decline. I see eq in a years time to be doing another round of server mergers. And I am sure they will claim they have 400,000 subscribers. Lets face it, they have to go to a bank and or investors for money to fund new games, and they need strong numbers to secure those debts.</td>
