						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">Tiiden .. bro you have just lost it.. I honestly can not believe the junk you are carrying on about ..as far as rylden talking down to the people I played with.. I dont like it one bit because they were good people.I don&#039;t care if he is a full member of the KKK. I will defend them to the end.You really need to come down off you high horse. You beat a few zones in a computer game.Great.. but to trash the people who played with you and were your friends. man.. <br /><br />As for me being an officer.. I do remember busting my tail trying to get peeps reflagged/taking attendance/recruiting when most of the other officers were not on.It was a full time reflag. So for about a month there I was getting it done bro.It was me and ysabeau as ONLY active officers holding the guild together when FOT, and ascent were taking a bite out of our player base.And if it had not been for justyse, jeddah and calsedon lending a hand, I dont know if I could have mustered enough hours during the day to get it done.But you know what, we did, and I got extremely tired of it.So sue me!<br /><br />On top of it all the, The suggestions in the officers forum I would make were all qickly opposed with the influx of all the new officers. I could not even get the guild excited about TRYING to attempt zones.IE ikkins 4 and uqua.I log in to &quot;help&quot; and I see everyone flagging for VP.I log out for at least 2 weeks so I dont interfere because I was highly oppsed to taking the guild to farm for inferrior loots.And when I saw the post about us going back to fire and farming fire after we had a time guild .. I got very vocal in the officer section.I guess you can sum it up as progression was a nasty word to even suggest.If we failed something once, it was taboo..You know I remember us getting ikkins 4  guy down to like 25ish with 4 clerics and because we failed we would not go back.You know good and well now looking back if we had a few more clerics and the proper kitting being done we would have owned that place.And as far as uqua.. it isn&#039;t that bad of a place now that everyone is level 70.<br /><br />I stayed off line for about a month to let you guys try and see that going backwards was not the solution to the problems of the guild.I played dota with smalls in vent of which I donated a VERY large portion of the yearly contract.I did NOT go into chat with other peeps.I think zubb logged in the channel one time and told me to hang in there and that you guys were gonna try and get things together during the transition which I did for several weeks and appreciated zubbs encouragement.<br /><br />But after seeing the post about going back to fire, I could not just sit there and do nothing.I had to speak my mind to try and save the other guys the let down of going BACK to fire.Ysabeau fully supported you guys about going back to fire .. so I /guildremoved and started playing eq again.I honestly do not think I was being booted from the guild.I feel very certian that I could have logged in and played with the conviction tag as an officer, but instead of trying to motivate you guys into trying to progress.. I guildremoved.Fact tiiden.. I left conviction.I did not get booted.There were some people who encouraged me to come back, and I really hated leaving because I had some really good friends in conviction.It was one of the hardest things I had to do in eq.<br /><br />I am NOT taking any credit for anything conviction did in its progression.I am sooo happy things are doing well for you all.I think you guys as officers have really stuck it out and work hard on getting peeps geared, and I think it is great.I do Know that there are alot of people in the guild that are either &quot;old&quot; members or flagged by &quot;old&quot; conviction members.It takes nothing away from the accomplishments of what you guys have achieved.Great job.But if I were you I would not be as head strong in thanking disso and crew for getting you guys a long way to where you are now.<br /><br />You know tiiden .. it was me who suggested you as an officer to conviction.I thought you would be the most perfect person for the job.I have NO clue why in the world you would even want to come here and give me grief.<br /></td>
